</previous_versions>

Call the tool with `data` containing one entry:
- `clause_title`: "Dispute Resolution"
- `summary`: "Establishes a tiered dispute resolution mechanism beginning with executive negotiation, escalating to non-binding mediation, while preserving each party's right to seek injunctive relief in court for breaches of confidentiality."
- `content`: "The parties shall first attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of or relating to this Agreement (a \"Dispute\") through direct negotiation between executives with authority to settle, for a period of not less than {{negotiation_period}} following written notice of the Dispute. If the Dispute remains unresolved at the conclusion of such negotiation period, the parties shall submit the matter to non-binding mediation administered by {{mediation_provider}}, seated in {{mediation_seat}}, with the costs of mediation borne equally by the parties. Nothing in this clause shall prevent either party from seeking immediate injunctive, declaratory, or other equitable relief in a court of competent jurisdiction located in {{equitable_relief_jurisdiction}} to enforce its rights under the confidentiality and non-use provisions of this Agreement, and the parties consent to the personal jurisdiction of such courts for that limited purpose."

<!-- Both prior versions used binding arbitration in a single paragraph. The new version varies on legal mechanism (arbitration → tiered negotiation/mediation) and structural approach (single arbitration paragraph → multi-step escalation with carve-out for court equitable relief) — two axes changed, satisfying the regeneration rule. -->
</example_regeneration>
</examples>
